{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1340 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "306cbc66e602f1ddf92a6d7b348c8b32c7a596d7a9f9f9270f8d00cbb918e7fe" :edb/db-before-t 1339 :edb/db-after-t 1340 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534652 50 #inst "2026-10-08T03:16:11.757Z" 13194139534652 true] [17592186096753 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301517 13194139534652 true] [17592186096753 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301524 13194139534652 true] [17592186096753 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301531 13194139534652 true] [17592186096753 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301534 13194139534652 true] [17592186096754 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301510 13194139534652 true] [17592186096754 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301548 13194139534652 true] [17592186096755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301537 13194139534652 true] [17592186096755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301541 13194139534652 true] [17592186096755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301555 13194139534652 true] [17592186096976 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534652 true] [17592186096976 1100 "Calculate $\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534652 true] [17592186096976 1100 "Calculate $\\intx\\log_{2} (3x)dx$." 13194139534652 false] [17592186096976 1145 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\cdot (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(3x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301510 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301511 13194139534652 true] [17592186301510 1089 "q-12566" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301510 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534652 true] [17592186301510 1100 "Calculate $\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301510 1113 #uuid "acfabbf7-741d-5b7a-a2d2-0388e3cd4c2f" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301510 1145 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}={x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{2}⁡(x))(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301511 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301512 13194139534652 true] [17592186301511 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301513 13194139534652 true] [17592186301511 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301514 13194139534652 true] [17592186301511 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301515 13194139534652 true] [17592186301511 1000 #edb/ref 1759