swer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}4{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301531 1113 #uuid "12fdbac6-b0fe-5529-b377-32ed7d4fe6fd" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301531 1145 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4{x}^{5} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 4{x}^{5}\\,dx=\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}4{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}(\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\frac{2({e}^{3})^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})}{3}-\\frac{2(1)^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)}{3}]-\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{18}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{6}}{9}{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{18}-(\\frac{{e}^{18}}{9}-\\frac{1}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(18{e}^{18}-{e}^{18}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(17{e}^{18}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301532 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301533 13194139534652 true] [17592186301532 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534652 true] [17592186301532 1041 "field-1" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301532 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301533 13194139534652 true] [17592186301532 1110 #uuid "5578b927-5d8c-5e1d-9eaa-a72aab5a6f04" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301533 1034 "\\frac{17e^{18}+1}{9}" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301533 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534652 true] [17592186301533 1111 #uuid "239eed72-3016-52bd-9509-b0b5ff978706" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301534 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301535 13194139534652 true] [17592186301534 1089 "q-350965" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301534 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534652 true] [17592186301534 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}4{x}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301534 1113 #uuid "b7a04644-a966-560d-8fe0-a0cecdf92a78" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301534 1145 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4{x}^{6} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 4{x}^{6}\\,dx=\\frac{4{x}^{7}}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}4{x}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{4{x}^{7}}{7}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}(\\frac{4{x}^{7}}{7})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\frac{4({e}^{2})^{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})}{7}-\\frac{4(1)^{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)}{7}]-\\frac{4}{7}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}{x}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4{e}^{14}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})}{7}-\\frac{4{x}^{7}}{49}{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8{e}^{14}}{7}-(\\frac{4{e}^{14}}{49}-\\frac{4}{49}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{49}(56{e}^{14}-4{e}^{14}+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{49}(13{e}^{14}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301535 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301536 13194139534652 true] [17592186301535 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534652 true] [17592186301535 1041 "field-1" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301535 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301536 13194139534652 true] [17592186301535 1110 #uuid "836698fc-7f29-5146-8d66-1ef9cfde66fe" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301536 1034 "\\frac{52e^{14}+4}{49}" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301536 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534652 true] [17592186301536 1111 #uuid "ad9ad490-8d79-549f-9c25-d17ebabe1e14" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301537 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301538 13194139534652 true] [17592186301537 1089 "q-350967" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301537 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534652 true] [17592186301537 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301537 1113 #uuid "01434e96-0acb-5606-b679-13b67a626150" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301537 1145 "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 1\\cdot \\,dx=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1/2}^{e/2}-{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,(x){|}_{1/2}^{e/2}-{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}x(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{e}{2})\\,(\\frac{e}{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})\\,(\\frac{1}{2})]-{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)-x{|}_{1/2}^{e/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}e-\\frac{1}{2}e+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301539 13194139534652 true] [17592186301538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301540 13194139534652 true] [17592186301538 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534652 true] [17592186301538 1041 "field-1" 13194139534652 true] [17592186301538 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301540 13194139534652 true] [17592186301538 1110 #uu